    THE HONEST READING: (b) is BUILT FROM (a)'s own measurements' normalizations --
    the consensus curve passes through the GAMA/MaNGA/zCOSMOS rows by construction
    (G150 Part 2, V2) -- so (b) vs the data is trivially consistent; (c) sits within
    +-6% of unity at the centroid masses (the SHMR-NFW head-to-head is sub-10% at
    10-30 kpc, M* - 2e11); (a) = (b) x (c) therefore ALSO sits within a few percent
    of the measurements in the 10-30 kpc decade: the CENTROID IS NOT THE TEST.
    The testable signal is the CORNER: (a)/(b) = 1 + delta_direct = 0.48-0.60 (a
    40-52% deficit) ONLY in the light-member 40-60 kpc corner -- the one window no
    published point occupies.  The MaNGA/GAMA data at 40-60 kpc:
